      "description": "Two hundred feet east of this highway is the tomb of\nMARY WYATT WHITAKER\nBORN AT TALLAHASSEE, FLORIDA, APRIL 11, 1831\nDaughter of William Wyatt, member of the Convention which gave to the State of Florida its first Constitution;\nMother of the first white child born in what is now Sarasota County, April 19, 1852.\nThree hundred yards west of this highway stood her home which was burned in 1856 by Indians, from whom she fled for safety with the child to a palmetto log fort on Manatee River.\nThis marker was erected in 1936 by the SARA DE SOTO CHAPTER\n\nDaughters of the American Revolution.",
